gned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x) & ={2}^{3} \\\\  & =8 \\\\  & =f(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=2$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & =2(2)^{2} \\\\  & =8 \\\\  & =f(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function is both left and right-continuous at $x=2,$ which implies that the function is continuous at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042135/state.json" "file_sha256" "388a8e5b40a8eee77b9b6e5c872fbe9cc20cdf78f22584b7cc618c32262b3c54"} {"question" "q-104384" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042135/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "085e0c4962b08f5af8d57216626efe3abb2a896cc7a82086a8c07947eb358e2e"} {"question" "q-104384" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042135/state.json" "file_sha256" "388a8e5b40a8eee77b9b6e5c872fbe9cc20cdf78f22584b7cc618c32262b3c54"} {"question" "q-104384" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042135/state.json" "file_sha256" "388a8e5b40a8eee77b9b6e5c872fbe9cc20cdf78f22584b7cc618c32262b3c54"} {"question" "q-104384" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "ca