determine the left and right continuity properties of $h(x)$ at $x=0.$\n\nFirst, we note that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(0) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is left-continuous at $x=0$ since the left-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}h(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-0) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =0 \\\\  & =h(0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=0$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}h(x) & =-2(0)^{2} \\\\  & =0 \\\\  & =h(0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function is both left and right-continuous at $x=0,$ which implies that the function is continuous at $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042135/state.json" "file_sha256" "388a8e5b40a8eee77b9b6e5c872fbe9cc20cdf78f22584b7cc618c32262b3c54"} {"question" "q-141012" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042135/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "085e0c4962b08f5af8d57216626efe3abb2a896cc7a82086a8c07947eb358e2e"} {"question" "q-141012" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042135/state.json" "file_sha256" "388a8e5b40a8eee77b9b6e5c872fbe9cc20cdf78f22584b7cc618c32262b3c54"} {"question" "q-141012" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None 