d{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. For the function to be continuous at $x=-1,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not left-continuous at $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042135/state.json" "file_sha256" "388a8e5b40a8eee77b9b6e5c872fbe9cc20cdf78f22584b7cc618c32262b3c54"} {"question" "q-141017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042135/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "085e0c4962b08f5af8d57216626efe3abb2a896cc7a82086a8c07947eb358e2e"} {"question" "q-141017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042135/state.json" "file_sha256" "388a8e5b40a8eee77b9b6e5c872fbe9cc20cdf78f22584b7cc618c32262b3c54"} {"question" "q-141017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042135/state.json" "file_sha256" "388a8e5b40a8eee77b9b6e5c872fbe9cc20cdf78f22584b7cc618c32262b3c54"} {"question" "q-141017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042135/state.json" "file_sha256" "388a8e5b40a8eee77b9b6e5c872fbe9cc20cdf78f22584b7cc618c32262b3c54"} {"question" "e-9965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $h(x),$ defined below?\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042135/assets/ba95d95494b67b2da7f5ebeb108fd75a42945291bae5440ff12d2edaa73f2798.png)\n\n- $h(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=1$\n\n- $h(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=1$\n\n- $h(x)$ is continuous at $x=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042135/example-9965.json" "file_sha256" "e420b16a13cc82e858f96356fe356f8045b84183f14baf35009465ce9424eabb"} {"question" "e-9965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're required to determine the left and right continuity properties of $h(x)$ at $x = 1.$\n\nLet's start by computing $h(1){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(1) & ={e}^{1-1} \\\\  & ={e}^{0} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is left-continuous at $x=1$ since the left-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}h(x) & ={e}^{1-1} \\\\  & ={e}^{0} \\\\  & =1 \\\\  & =h(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is *not* right-continuous at $x=1$ since the right-sided limit is *not* equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}h(x) & =1-1 \\\\  & =0 \\\\  & \\ne h(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStatement III is false. For the function to be continuous at $x=1,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous at this point. However, we have already determined that the function is not right-continuous at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042135/example-9965.json" "file_sha256" "e420b16a13cc82e858f96356fe356f